refentry.refsect1:
&reftitle.parameters;
timestamp
Unix timestamp representing the date. A &float; value is also accepted which allows for microsecond precision.

&reftitle.errors;

 If the timestamp is outside the range [PHP_INT_MIN, PHP_INT_MAX],
 a DateRangeError is thrown.

  &reftitle.examples;

   DateTime::createFromTimestamp example


<?php
$date = DateTime::createFromTimestamp(123.456789);
echo $date->format('Y-m-d H:i:s.u');
?>


   &example.outputs;


1970-01-01 00:02:03.456789




   Converting the result to the default timezone


<?php
date_default_timezone_set('Europe/Amsterdam');

$date = DateTime::createFromTimestamp(1700000000);
echo $date->format('Y-m-d H:i:s P e'), "\n";

$date->setTimezone(new DateTimeZone(date_default_timezone_get()));
echo $date->format('Y-m-d H:i:s P e'), "\n";
?>


   &example.outputs;


2023-11-14 22:13:20 +00:00 +00:00
2023-11-14 23:13:20 +01:00 Europe/Amsterdam
